ter incision  put the old dressing in a plastic bag  and throw it into the waste basket  step 4 remove your disposable gloves and  throw them away in the waste basket  step 5 wash your hands again with soap  and water and then dry them  step 6 put on disposable gloves  step 7 wash the skin around your  incision using a washcloth and warm  soapy water dry your skin completely  with a clean paper towel  [Music]  step 8 wash about 4 inches of the  catheter tube where it enters your skin  with a cotton swab or ball and warm  soapy water  [Music]  start at your incision and wipe away  from your body  do not wipe toward your incision  step nine  place a new four inch by four inch split  dressing gauze at your incision and  around the catheter tube  tape the gauze in place using dressing  tape  [Music]  be sure to clean your suprapubic  catheter at least once a day  contact your surgeon if  you have any questions about your  suprapubic catheter you have chills and  your temperature is 101 degrees  fahrenheit or higher  your bladder feels full but you see no  urine draining into the bag  your incision is bleeding or swollen  urine is leaking around your catheter  your urine is cloudy has a foul odor you  see grit or stones in your urine or you  notice bright red blood in your urine  it is normal to see a small amount of  blood or pink tinged urine after some  procedures  [Music]
 

